    <%# EJS DOCUMENTATION: https://ejs.co/ %>
    COMMENT: ====================================================================================
    COMMENT: CUSTOM PROPERTIES FOR Execute OBJECT
    COMMENT: ====================================================================================
    
    COMMENT: Internal reference to the component being executed
    PRIVATE componentModel: BaseComponent
        PURPOSE: Stores the component model instance that will be executed
        WHY: Execute objects wrap components for queuing and batch execution
    
    COMMENT: NOTE: The following properties are set automatically by setComponent()
    COMMENT: They don't need explicit property definitions unless required by your language
    
    COMMENT: component: String
    COMMENT:     The name of the component being executed (e.g., "Medal.unlock")
    COMMENT:     Derived from: componentModel.objectName (the full "Component.method"
    COMMENT:     path - this is the string the gateway routes on)
    
    COMMENT: parameters: Object
    COMMENT:     The component's plain, unencrypted parameters
    COMMENT:     Derived from: componentModel.toObject() -- set once, in setComponent(),
    COMMENT:     regardless of whether the component is secure

    COMMENT: secure: String
    COMMENT:     Declared by the schema, but never assigned directly on this model. Whether
    COMMENT:     the outgoing wire entry ends up as {component, parameters} or as a
    COMMENT:     {secure: encryptedString} wrapper is a serialize-time decision made by the
    COMMENT:     request helper (see methods.ejs), not something this class computes and
    COMMENT:     stores on itself.

